Any two distinct clients diverge at one of the tree’s three arbitration levels. The lemmas below connect a locking client to its acknowledged path, then establish that each cell acknowledges at most one child. Together, they make mutual exclusion a one-step consequence, assuming a rising-edge reset establishes the initial state. The explicit clock and reset-disable form follows concurrent SVA syntax. ([accellera.org](https://www.accellera.org/images/resources/videos/SystemVerilog_Assertions_Tutorial_2016.pdf))

<json>
{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (({(P7_state == 2'd2), (P6_state == 2'd2), (P5_state == 2'd2), (P4_state == 2'd2), (P3_state == 2'd2), (P2_state == 2'd2), (P1_state == 2'd2), (P0_state == 2'd2)} & ~a0) == 8'b0); endproperty",
      "explanation": "A process enters locking only after its leaf acknowledgment, and keeps requesting until it leaves locking. Thus every locking client retains its leaf acknowledgment."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (((a0[1:0] == 2'b00) || a1[0]) && ((a0[3:2] == 2'b00) || a1[1]) && ((a0[5:4] == 2'b00) || a1[2]) && ((a0[7:6] == 2'b00) || a1[3])); endproperty",
      "explanation": "A leaf cell can acknowledge a client only while its parent acknowledges that cell. Its asserted request holds the parent acknowledgment for as long as needed."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (((a1[1:0] == 2'b00) || a2[0]) && ((a1[3:2] == 2'b00) || a2[1])); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The same request-and-acknowledgment persistence carries each middle-level acknowledgment to its root-cell acknowledgment."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_4; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (!(a0[0] && a0[1]) && !(a0[2] && a0[3]) && !(a0[4] && a0[5]) && !(a0[6] && a0[7])); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Each leaf cell has one state register, so its ack1 and ack2 outputs cannot both be asserted. This excludes two locking clients in the same leaf pair."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_5; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) (!(a1[0] && a1[1]) && !(a1[2] && a1[3])); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Each middle-level cell acknowledges at most one leaf cell. With lemma_2, this excludes simultaneous locks in different leaf pairs under the same middle-level cell."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_6; @(posedge clk) disable iff (rst) !(a2[0] && a2[1]); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The root cell acknowledges at most one half of the tree. With lemmas_1 through lemma_5, this excludes the remaining pairs of simultaneous locking clients."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

